cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SHERLOC in your research, please cite the manuscript and this software."
title: "SHERLOC: an interpretable deep-learning model of longitudinal ctDNA for calibrated early treatment monitoring in advanced breast cancer (PADA-1) and non-small-cell lung cancer (IMpower150)"
abstract: >-
  SHERLOC (Shared and Exclusive Representations of Longitudinal ctDNA) is an
  interpretable deep Cox model for short longitudinal ctDNA trajectories in
  clinical trials. A temporal kernel shared by all gene-level VAFs, one
  temporal map per panel-level feature, and a genomic-interaction encoder
  pre-trained on MSK-CHORD and frozen feed a Cox layer with one coefficient per
  representation; the risk score is recalibrated out of fold into calibrated
  survival probabilities. Applied to PADA-1 and IMpower150.
